  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let f(X)f(X)f(X) denote the number of set bits in XXX.\n\nGiven integers NNN and KKK, construct an array AAA of length NNN such that:\n\n\n0≤Ai≤K0 \\leq A_i \\leq K0≤Ai​≤K for all (1≤i≤N)(1 \\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N);\n∑i=1NAi=K\\sum_{i=1}^{N} A_i = K∑i=1N​Ai​=K\nOver all such possible arrays, find the **maximum** value of ∑i=1Nf(Ai)\\sum_{i=1}^{N} f(A_i)∑i=1N​f(Ai​).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follow.\nThe only line of each test case contains integers NNN and KKK- the length of the array and sum of elements respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the **maximum** value of ∑i=1Nf(Ai)\\sum_{i=1}^{N} f(A_i)∑i=1N​f(Ai​).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1091 \\leq N \\leq 10^91≤N≤109",
      "0≤K≤1090 \\leq K \\leq 10^90≤K≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n1 7\n3 6",
        "output": "3\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Only one array is possible that is A=[7]A =[7]A=[7]. As 7=(111)27 = (111)_27=(111)2​, the number of set bits in 777 is 333. Thus, ∑i=1Nf(Ai)=f(7)=3\\sum_{i=1}^{N} f(A_i) = f(7) = 3∑i=1N​f(Ai​)=f(7)=3.\nTest case 222: A possible array satisfying all the conditions is A=[3,0,3]A =[3, 0, 3]A=[3,0,3]. As 3=(11)23 = (11)_23=(11)2​, the number of set bits in 333 is 222. Similarly, the number of set bits in 000 is 000. Thus, ∑i=1Nf(Ai)=f(3)+f(0)+f(3)=4\\sum_{i=1}^{N} f(A_i) = f(3) + f(0) + f(3) = 4∑i=1N​f(Ai​)=f(3)+f(0)+f(3)=4. It can be proven that answer never exceeds 444."
      }
    ]
  },
